# Sources: Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions,
# ch. 5, pp. 250–267; official Majles proceedings, session 30, 1 June 1950.
# Mechanical effects are counterfactual abstractions.
title: <span class="term term-makki">Hossein Makki</span>
new-page: true
is-pinned-card: true
tags: advisor
view-if: advisor_makki_available = 1

= {!<span class="term term-makki">!}Hossein Makki{!</span>!}

{!<span class="term term-makki">!}Makki{!</span>!} is a politician and oil
advocate who has joined the common election protest around
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}. Before the
Sixteenth {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} convenes,
his intervention is public and electoral rather than parliamentary.

- @makki_floor
- @makki_oil
- @makki_questions
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@makki_floor
title: Prepare a public intervention
subtitle: <span class="term term-makki">Makki</span> turns <span class="term term-mossadegh">Mossadegh</span>'s constitutional position into a case that demands an answer
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; mossadegh_authority += 2

{!<span class="term term-makki">!}Makki{!</span>!} prepares the order of
claims and documents, then coordinates the handoff between speakers. The plan
keeps the constitutional case visible alongside the political demand.

[? if majles_convened = 0: The protest gains a disciplined public argument
without claiming a parliamentary floor that does not yet exist. ?]
[? if majles_convened = 1:
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} deputies enter
the chamber with a clearer division of work. ?]
In either setting,
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mossadegh{!</span>!}'s role in holding that work together becomes more credible.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@makki_oil
title: Rally support on oil
subtitle: The appeal asks deputies and the public to choose national control before every term is settled
view-if: oil_committee_formed = 1
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and oil_committee_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; oil_coalition_support += 5; public_mandate += 2

{!<span class="term term-makki">!}Makki{!</span>!} identifies deputies who can be moved on oil without asking them to join
the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} or endorse
its whole program. He supplies the press with the same
limited question so that parliamentary outreach and public advocacy reinforce
one another.

Support for the oil campaign grows. Agreement on the principle does not settle
every term of implementation.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@makki_questions
title: Prepare a committee examination
subtitle: Each question forces the agreement's defenders to name who owns, operates, markets, and pays
view-if: oil_committee_formed = 1
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and oil_committee_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; oil_coalition_support += 2

{!<span class="term term-makki">!}Makki{!</span>!} turns the proposal comparison into a sequence of committee questions:
who owns, who operates, who markets, who appoints, and what remains reviewable.
Unknown provisions are left open rather than answered for the government.

The examination gives the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} a stronger
procedural record and makes evasive answers more visible. It does not
guarantee the committee's conclusion.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing
